    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our clear focal point. Boasting a dominant 80.13 score, he benefits from an optimal leadoff spot against Dobbins, with a significant 14% boost stemming from a favorable dynamic platoon split. While **Yordan Alvarez** (62.19) and **Kyle Schwarber** (61.18) provide high-floor production, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains our primary engine for the scarce stolen base category, which remains the cornerstone of our strategy as we approach the final stretch of the season. **Junior Caminero** (60.55) rounds out our \"Strong\" tier, leveraging his excellent 0.373 xwOBA and an aggressive third-spot placement to overcome a stiff matchup against Rogers.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Dillon Dingler**, who missed the 40.0 efficiency threshold by less than three points. Despite the park factor favoring him against Burke, the negative drag from his dynamic platoon and the SP skill adjustment kept him firmly on the bench in favor of **Gary Sanchez**, who despite facing a tough Skubal, maintains enough baseline projection to clear our floor. We are exercising caution with **Gary Sanchez** and **Kazuma Okamoto** as they face formidable arms, but their projected volume secures their spots. We are closely monitoring weather reports, though no immediate risks have been flagged that would necessitate a late-scratch pivot for **Caleb Durbin** or **Colt Keith**. We continue to hold **Trea Turner** and **Christian Yelich** on the bench in anticipation of their return to active, high-leverage roles, as our current depth allows us to prioritize today\u2019s matchup-specific efficiencies over theoretical upside.",
